Third-party libraries used by a build
-------------------------------------

None of these are stored in this repository. Gradle downloads them, and they end up inside a
built APK:

  - AndroidX Media3 (ExoPlayer, UI) 1.6.1, Apache License 2.0.
    https://github.com/androidx/media
  - libVLC for Android (org.videolan.android:libvlc-all) 3.6.5, GNU LGPL 2.1 (as declared by
    its Maven POM; bundled VLC modules and libraries carry their own licences).
    https://code.videolan.org/videolan/vlc-android
  - Jellyfin Media3 FFmpeg decoder (org.jellyfin.media3:media3-ffmpeg-decoder) 1.6.1+2,
    GNU GPL 3.0 (as declared by its Maven POM). It contains a build of FFmpeg.
    https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-androidx-media
  - Kotlin standard library 1.9.24, Apache License 2.0.

Because the Jellyfin FFmpeg decoder is GPL-3.0, an APK built from this repository as it is
must be distributed under the terms of the GNU GPL, version 3, as a whole. The source in this
repository is compatible with that: Apache-2.0 code may be combined into a GPL-3.0 work, and
the LGPL-2.1-or-later files may be conveyed under the GPL. Whoever distributes such an APK
must offer its complete corresponding source (this repository at the matching commit, plus
the exact dependency versions from app/build.gradle) and the GPL-3.0 licence text.

Built-in torrent engine (TorrServer)
------------------------------------

A built APK contains lib/<abi>/libtorrserver.so, a build of TorrServer:

    TorrServer, https://github.com/YouROK/TorrServer
    Copyright YouROK and the TorrServer contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0).

It is a separate program, not a library: Kino starts it as a child process and talks to it
over HTTP on 127.0.0.1 only. Kino's own code stays under Apache-2.0.

  torrserver/upstream   git submodule: upstream TorrServer at the pinned commit (the tag is in
                        torrserver/VERSION), not modified in place
  torrserver/patches    our changes, GPL-3.0 like the code they modify: a "kino" build tag that
                        leaves out the web UI, Swagger, MCP, MSX, WebDAV, FUSE and the Telegram
                        bot
  torrserver/build.sh   applies the patches and builds the program for arm64-v8a and
                        armeabi-v7a with the Android NDK (build tags nosqlite, kino, nomsgpack)

TorrServer pulls in Go modules under their own licences (among them anacrolix/torrent,
MPL-2.0; gin, MIT; bbolt, MIT). Every Kino release from the one that first ships the engine
has torrserver-<version>-src.tar.gz attached: the complete corresponding source of the
program inside the APK (upstream tree with the patches applied, all Go modules vendored,
this build script). Prebuilt GStreamer libraries for desktop systems
(server/gstreamer/gst-libs) are left out of it because this build does not use them.
